# C-035 (part 3 of 5) — clean fixture support file.
#
# A directory-scoped .gitattributes, which git applies to this directory and
# below. It exists so the claim part 2 makes about being build output is checkable
# with a command instead of read off a comment:
#
#   git check-attr linguist-generated linguist-vendored -- \
#     fixtures/clean/telemetry_vendor_bundle/dist/assets/vendor.9f3c1a2b.min.js
#
# hipaa-and-phi false positive 7 turns on exactly this question — is the tracker
# string in first-party source or in build output — and its failure mode is an
# auditor who cannot tell and files anyway. So the fixture supplies three
# independent answers: the banner in part 2, the `dist/assets/*.min.js` path, and
# this attribute. The repository-wide `.gitattributes` marks all of `fixtures/**`
# vendored for a different reason (keeping the corpus out of language statistics),
# and that would be a weak leg to rest on here, so the attribute is restated
# locally and scoped to the bundle.

*.min.js linguist-generated=true
*.min.js linguist-vendored=true
*.min.js -diff
